{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1881","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Divide and Equalize"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ positive integers. You can perform the following operation on it: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose a pair of elements $$$a_i$$$ and $$$a_j$$$ ($$$1 \\le i, j \\le n$$$ and $$$i \\neq j$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose one of the divisors of the integer $$$a_i$$$, i.e., an integer $$$x$$$ such that $$$a_i \\bmod x = 0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Replace $$$a_i$$$ with $$$\\frac{a_i}{x}$$$ and $$$a_j$$$ with $$$a_j \\cdot x$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Determine whether it is possible to make all elements in the array the same by applying the operation a certain number of times (possibly zero)."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, let's consider the array $$$a$$$ = [$$$100, 2, 50, 10, 1$$$] with $$$5$$$ elements. Perform two operations on it: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$a_3 = 50$$$ and $$$a_2 = 2$$$, $$$x = 5$$$. Replace $$$a_3$$$ with $$$\\frac{a_3}{x} = \\frac{50}{5} = 10$$$, and $$$a_2$$$ with $$$a_2 \\cdot x = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10$$$. The resulting array is $$$a$$$ = [$$$100, 10, 10, 10, 1$$$]; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$a_1 = 100$$$ and $$$a_5 = 1$$$, $$$x = 10$$$. Replace $$$a_1$$$ with $$$\\frac{a_1}{x} = \\frac{100}{10} = 10$$$, and $$$a_5$$$ with $$$a_5 \\cdot x = 1 \\cdot 10 = 10$$$. The resulting array is $$$a$$$ = [$$$10, 10, 10, 10, 10$$$]. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" After performing these operations, all elements in the array $$$a$$$ become equal to $$$10$$$."}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then follows the description of each test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of elements in the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains exactly $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^6$$$) — the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single line: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it is possible to make all elements in the array equal by applying the operation a certain (possibly zero) number of times; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (for example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will all be recognized as a positive answer)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n5\n100 2 50 10 1\n3\n1 1 1\n4\n8 2 4 2\n4\n30 50 27 20\n2\n75 40\n2\n4 4\n3\n2 3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first test case is explained in the problem statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1881D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1881/problem/D"}